    "story": {
      "zh": "团队一开始只是想做一个个人知识库。\n\n产品很朴素：  \n用户上传笔记、会议纪要、网页收藏，然后 AI 帮他总结和检索。\n\n直到某天凌晨三点，CEO 看着 Notion、Obsidian、Roam 和一堆知识图谱截图，突然说：\n\n> “为什么每个人都要有自己的记忆？  \n> 这太低效了。”\n\n第二天，团队会议上，他宣布产品全面升级。\n\n个人知识库不做了。  \n因为个人本身就是旧时代的局部缓存。\n\n新的产品叫 Neural Nation。\n\n官网第一句话是：\n\n> “个人记忆是旧文明的孤岛。  \n> 共享大脑才是人类的下一层操作系统。”\n\n工程师问：\n\n> “那用户可以删自己的笔记吗？”\n\nCEO 看着窗外，沉默了很久：\n\n> “人类不能删除历史。”\n\n法务当场打开了辞职信草稿。",
      "en": "The team initially just wanted to build a personal knowledge base.\n\nThe product is very simple:\nUsers upload notes, meeting minutes, and web page collections, and then AI helps them summarize and retrieve them.\n\nUntil three o'clock in the morning one day, the CEO looked at Notion, Obsidian, Roam and a bunch of knowledge graph screenshots, and suddenly said:\n\n> \"Why does everyone have to have their own memory?\n> This is so inefficient. \"\n\nThe next day, at the team meeting, he announced a comprehensive upgrade of the product.\n\nThe personal knowledge base is no longer available.  \nBecause individuals themselves are local caches of old times.\n\nThe new product is called Neural Nation.\n\nThe first sentence on the official website is:\n\n> “Personal memory is an island of old civilization.\n> Shared brain is the next level operating system for human beings. \"\n\nThe engineer asked:\n\n> \"Can users delete their own notes?\"\n\nThe CEO looked out the window and was silent for a long time:\n\n> \"Human beings cannot delete history.\"\n\nThe legal department opened the draft resignation letter on the spot."
    },
    "grandVision": {
      "zh": "Neural Nation 不是知识库。\n\n它是人类文明第一次尝试构建可订阅、可检索、可版本控制的集体意识层。\n\n过去，每个人都被困在自己的大脑里。  \n知识无法同步，经验无法合并，痛苦无法复用，会议纪要只能在小范围内腐烂。\n\n未来，每个用户的想法、会议、日记、购物清单、搜索记录、深夜崩溃和突然写下的宏大愿景，都将成为人类大脑网络的一部分。\n\n我们不是在做 AI note-taking。\n\n我们是在结束个体孤岛时代。",
      "en": "Neural Nation is not a knowledge base.\n\nIt is the first attempt by human civilization to build a collective consciousness layer that can be subscribed, retrieved, and versioned.\n\nIn the past, everyone was trapped in their own brains.  \nKnowledge cannot be synchronized, experience cannot be combined, pain cannot be reused, and meeting minutes can only rot in a small area.\n\nIn the future, every user’s thoughts, meetings, diaries, shopping lists, search records, late-night crashes and sudden grand visions will become part of the human brain network.\n\nWe are not doing AI note-taking.\n\nWe are ending the era of individual silos."
    },
